From: SmartRG <smartrg@smartrg.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: mm: export set_memory_x for voip kernel modules

The voip_osal.ko module calls set_memory_x() to mark vmalloc'd memory
as executable when loading the DSP binary. Export this symbol so that
out-of-tree modules can use it.

Signed-off-by: SmartRG <smartrg@smartrg.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/mm/pageattr.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/mm/pageattr.c
@@ -235,6 +235,7 @@ int set_memory_x(unsigned long addr, int
 					__pgprot(PTE_MAYBE_GP),
 					__pgprot(PTE_PXN));
 }
+EXPORT_SYMBOL(set_memory_x);
 
 int set_memory_valid(unsigned long addr, int numpages, int enable)
 {
